6.
Duties of the Principal Officer.
- The principal officer of the test centre has the following responsibilities, namely -
(i)
to establish and operate the test centre as an independent unit;
(ii)
to ensure that the staff of the test centre carry out their duties independently;
(iii)
to inform the Director, Legal Metrology in the Department of Consumer Affairs of cessation of operation of test centre;
(iv)
to maintain the accuracy of testing equipment as per rules and directions issued from time to time;
(v)
to maintain proper record of testing and certificates issued by Government Approved Test Centre;
(vi)
to record and redress grievances of customers in appropriate manner;
(vii)
to abide by the directions issued by Director (Legal Metrology) from time to time,
(viii)
only weights or measures conforming to specification are stamped;
(ix)
verification stamps are adequately protected against fraudulent use;
